IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa3-part8-members`

-- coa3-part8-inspection.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 8, Chapter 2 from s 114 to the end of the Chapter
-- (inspection, copies, removal of entries, special cases, rectification, evidence, time limit) and Chapter 2A (blank in
-- this text): ss 114 to 128ZA, 128A to 128K; lines 1532-1713 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. See coa3-part8-members.l4 for how to read JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING.
-- It calls `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` from
-- coa3-part8-members.l4 for the limbs "(a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default".
--
-- SEAMS taken as INPUTS: s 1(1) the body is a company; s 1121 the officer is in default; s 724 (treasury shares) applies;
-- s 1080 the register kept by the registrar; s 1081(1A) the date recorded by the registrar; s 1136 (the place in regulations);
-- s 1173(1) working days (the person counts them); s 120A restrictions (a flag, the regulations are not in the sources).

DECLARE `s 114 act under Chapter 2 of Part 8` IS ONE OF
    `s 114(2) the company gives notice to the registrar of the place where the register is kept`
    `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request`
    `s 117(1)(b) the company applies to the court`
    `s 117(2) the company notifies the person making the request`
    `s 120(1) the company informs the person of the most recent date of alteration`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- INSPECTION ETC OF REGISTER AND INDEX OF MEMBERS (ss 114 to 120B)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 114: the register is kept available for inspection ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1534 | (1) A company's register of members must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:1535 | (a) at its registered office, or
-- src:1536 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 114(1) The places where the register may be kept (src:1534-1536)
DECLARE `s 114(1) place where the register is kept` IS ONE OF
    `s 114(1)(a) at its registered office`
    `s 114(1)(b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136`
    `s 114(1) at another place`

-- gloss: the register must be at the registered office or at a place the regulations name; the right to inspect it is in s 116.
-- src:1533 | 114 Register to be kept available for inspection
-- src:1534 | (1) A company's register of members must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:1535 | (a) at its registered office, or
-- src:1536 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
-- src:1537 | This is subject to any restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material).
@ref s 114(1) Register to be kept available for inspection (src:1533-1537)
GIVEN place IS A `s 114(1) place where the register is kept`
      `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114(1) the register of members is kept at a place that satisfies s 114(1)` MEANS
    IF `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "This is subject to any restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material)"; those regulations are not among the sources
    ELSE CONSIDER place
         WHEN `s 114(1)(a) at its registered office` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 114(1)(b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 114(1) at another place` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company's register of members must be kept available for inspection— (a) at its registered office, or (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136" (a duty that names two places; fork F8)

-- src:1538 | (2) A company must give notice to the registrar of the place where its register of members is kept available for inspection and of any change in that place.
@ref s 114(2) Notice to the registrar of the place (src:1538)
GIVEN `s 1(1) the body is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place where its register is kept available and of any change in that place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1(1) the body is a company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company must give notice"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1(1) "unless the context otherwise requires"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The text fixes no time in s 114(2); the 14 days are in s 114(5) (default for 14 days).
@ref s 114(2) Notice to the registrar of the place (src:1538)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 114 act under Chapter 2 of Part 8`
`s 114(2) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 114(2) the company gives notice to the registrar of the place where the register is kept`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not give notice to the registrar of the place where its register of members is kept"

-- gloss: no notice is needed for a register that has always been at the registered office; the "relevant date" is the day the
-- register may have existed since (s 114(4)).
-- src:1539 | (3) No such notice is required if the register has, at all times since it came into existence (or, in the case of a register in existence on the relevant date, at all times since then) been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office.
@ref s 114(3) No notice is required where the register has always been at the registered office (src:1539)
GIVEN `the register was in existence on the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register has at all times since it came into existence been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register has at all times since the relevant date been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114(3) no notice is required under s 114(2)` MEANS
    IF       (`the register was in existence on the relevant date` AND `the register has at all times since the relevant date been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office`)
         OR ((NOT `the register was in existence on the relevant date`) AND `the register has at all times since it came into existence been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No such notice is required if the register has, at all times since it came into existence (or, in the case of a register in existence on the relevant date, at all times since then) been kept available for inspection at the company's registered office" (the "if" does not hold)

-- src:1540 | (4) The relevant date for the purposes of subsection (3) is—
-- src:1541 | (a) 1st July 1948 in the case of a company registered in Great Britain, and
-- src:1542 | (b) 1st April 1961 in the case of a company registered in Northern Ireland.
@ref s 114(4) The relevant date (src:1540-1542)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 114(4) the relevant date for the purposes of s 114(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN Date 1 4 1961
    OTHERWISE Date 1 7 1948 -- "Great Britain" is England and Wales together with Scotland

-- src:1543 | (5) If a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by—
-- src:1544 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1545 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 114(5) Offence: default for 14 days in complying with s 114(2) (src:1543-1545)
GIVEN `the number of days for which the company has made default in complying with subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the number of days for which the company has made default in complying with subsection (2)` LESS THAN 14
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default for 14 days in complying with subsection (2), an offence is committed by"
    ELSE `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` person `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:1546 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 114(6) Penalty (src:1546)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 114(6) the penalty for an offence under s 114` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- ---- s 115: index of members (the second "Index of members" in the text: fork F2) ---------------------------------------

-- src:1547 | 115 Index of members
-- src:1548 | (1) Every company having more than 50 members must keep an index of the names of the members of the company, unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index.
@ref s 115(1) Index of members (the text also has s 113J with the same heading) (src:1547-1548)
GIVEN `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(1) the company must keep an index of the names of its members` MEANS
    IF `the number of members of the company` AT MOST 50
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every company having more than 50 members"
    ELSE IF `the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1549 | (2) The company must make any necessary alteration in the index within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made in the register of members.
@ref s 115(2) Alteration of the index within 14 days (src:1549)
GIVEN `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 115(2) the last day for making the alteration in the index` MEANS
    `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members` PLUS 14 -- "within 14 days after the date": the 14th day after it

@ref s 115(2) Alteration of the index within 14 days (src:1549)
GIVEN `s 115(1) the company must keep an index of the names of its members` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the necessary alteration is made in the index` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(2) the company made the necessary alteration in the index within 14 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 115(1) the company must keep an index of the names of its members`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the date on which the necessary alteration is made in the index` LESS THAN `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 115(2) counts from the register's alteration; an earlier alteration of the index is not mentioned
        ELSE IF `the date on which the necessary alteration is made in the index` AT MOST `s 115(2) the last day for making the alteration in the index` `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made in the register of members"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 115(2) speaks of "the index", which only s 115(1) requires
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 115(2) speaks of "the index", which only s 115(1) requires

-- src:1550 | (3) The index must contain, in respect of each member, a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found.
@ref s 115(3) What the index must contain (src:1550)
GIVEN `the index contains, in respect of the member, a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(3) the index meets the requirement of a sufficient indication for each member` MEANS
    IF `the index contains, in respect of the member, a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The index must contain, in respect of each member, a sufficient indication to enable the account of that member in the register to be readily found"

-- src:1551 | (4) The index must be at all times kept available for inspection at the same place as the register of members.
-- src:1552 | (4A) Subsection (4) is subject to any restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material).
@ref s 115(4) and (4A) The index must be kept available for inspection (src:1551-1552)
GIVEN `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(4) the index must at all times be kept available for inspection at the same place as the register, subject to s 115(4A)` MEANS
    IF `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsection (4) is subject to any restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material)"; the regulations are not among the sources
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1553 | (5) If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:1554 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1555 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 115(5) Offence (src:1553-1555)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 115` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `default is made in complying with section 115`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` person `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:1556 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 115(6) Penalty (src:1556)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 115(6) the penalty for an offence under s 115` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- ---- s 116: rights to inspect and require copies ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1557 | 116 Rights to inspect and require copies
-- src:1558 | (1) The register and the index of members' names must be open to the inspection—
-- src:1559 | (a) of any member of the company without charge, and
@ref s 116(1)(a) Rights to inspect: members, without charge (src:1557-1559)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(1)(a) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection without charge` MEANS
    IF `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsections (1) and (2) are subject to any restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material)"
    ELSE IF `the person is a member of the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of any member of the company without charge" (s 116(1)(b) deals with any other person)

-- src:1557 | 116 Rights to inspect and require copies
-- src:1560 | (b) of any other person on payment of such fee as may be prescribed.
@ref s 116(1)(b) Rights to inspect: any other person, on payment of the prescribed fee (src:1557 and src:1560)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person pays the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(1)(b) the register and the index of members' names must be open to the person's inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` MEANS
    IF `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsections (1) and (2) are subject to any restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material)"
    ELSE IF `the person is a member of the company`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of any other person" (a member is dealt with by s 116(1)(a))
         ELSE IF `the person pays the prescribed fee`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on payment of such fee as may be prescribed" ("on" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)); the fee is prescribed outside the sources

-- src:1561 | (2) Any person may require a copy of a company's register of members, or of any part of it, on payment of such fee as may be prescribed.
-- src:1562 | (2A) Subsections (1) and (2) are subject to any restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material).
@ref s 116(2) and (2A) The right to require a copy (src:1561-1562)
GIVEN `the person pays the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(2) the person may require a copy of the register of members or of any part of it` MEANS
    IF `a restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material) applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subsections (1) and (2) are subject to any restriction imposed by regulations under section 120A (protected material)"
    ELSE IF `the person pays the prescribed fee`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on payment of such fee as may be prescribed" ("on" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- src:1563 | (3) A person seeking to exercise either of the rights conferred by this section must make a request to the company to that effect.
@ref s 116(3) A request must be made (src:1563)
GIVEN `the person seeks to exercise a right conferred by section 116` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(3) the person must make a request to the company` MEANS
    IF `the person seeks to exercise a right conferred by section 116`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person seeking to exercise either of the rights conferred by this section"

-- The request: one field per limb of s 116(4), each name prefixed with the limb.
-- src:1564 | (4) The request must contain the following information—
-- src:1565 | (a) in the case of an individual, his name and address;
-- src:1566 | (b) in the case of an organisation, the name and address of an individual responsible for making the request on behalf of the organisation;
-- src:1567 | (c) the purpose for which the information is to be used; and
-- src:1568 | (d) whether the information will be disclosed to any other person, and if so—
-- src:1569 | (i) where that person is an individual, his name and address,
-- src:1570 | (ii) where that person is an organisation, the name and address of an individual responsible for receiving the information on its behalf, and
-- src:1571 | (iii) the purpose for which the information is to be used by that person.
@ref s 116(4) What the request must contain (src:1564-1571)
DECLARE `s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` HAS
    `s 116(4)(a)-(b) the person making the request is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 116(4)(a)-(b) the name and address of the individual (or of the individual responsible for making the request for an organisation) is given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 116(4)(c) the purpose for which the information is to be used is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 116(4)(d) the request says whether the information will be disclosed to any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 116(4)(d) the information will be disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 116(4)(d)(i)-(ii) the other person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 116(4)(d)(i)-(ii) the name and address of the other person (or of the individual responsible for receiving the information for an organisation) is given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 116(4)(d)(iii) the purpose for which the other person is to use the information is stated` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 116(4) What the request must contain (src:1564-1571)
GIVEN request IS A `s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(4) the request contains the information that s 116(4) requires` MEANS
    IF       request's `s 116(4)(a)-(b) the name and address of the individual (or of the individual responsible for making the request for an organisation) is given`
         AND request's `s 116(4)(c) the purpose for which the information is to be used is stated`
         AND request's `s 116(4)(d) the request says whether the information will be disclosed to any other person`
         AND (    (NOT request's `s 116(4)(d) the information will be disclosed to another person`)
              OR (    request's `s 116(4)(d)(i)-(ii) the name and address of the other person (or of the individual responsible for receiving the information for an organisation) is given`
                  AND request's `s 116(4)(d)(iii) the purpose for which the other person is to use the information is stated`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The request must contain the following information" (a duty that lists what the request contains; fork F8)

-- ---- s 117: the company's response to a request ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1572 | 117 Register of members: response to request for inspection or copy
-- src:1573 | (1) Where a company receives a request under section 116 (register of members: right to inspect and require copy), it must within five working days either—
-- src:1574 | (a) comply with the request, or
-- src:1575 | (b) apply to the court.
@ref s 117(1) Response to a request: within five working days (src:1572-1575)
GIVEN `the company has received a request under section 116` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(1) the company must within five working days either comply with the request or apply to the court` MEANS
    IF `the company has received a request under section 116`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company receives a request under section 116"

-- "within five working days": the working days are counted by the person (the calendar is s 1173(1), a seam of the keel).
-- The count is of working days after the day of receipt: 0 is the day of receipt, 5 is the fifth working day.
@ref s 117(1) Response to a request: within five working days (src:1573)
GIVEN `the number of working days from receipt of the request until the company complied or applied to the court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(1) the company acted within five working days` MEANS
    IF `the number of working days from receipt of the request until the company complied or applied to the court` LESS THAN 0
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not deal with a response before the request was received
    ELSE IF `the number of working days from receipt of the request until the company complied or applied to the court` AT MOST 5
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within five working days"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the clock counts working days from the receipt of the request (day 0). The two ways
-- of acting are alternatives (ROR): either one fulfils the duty.
@ref s 117(1) Response to a request: within five working days (src:1573-1575)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 114 act under Chapter 2 of Part 8`
`s 117(1) the company must within five working days comply with the request or apply to the court (duty)` MEANS
    (   PARTY Company
        MUST `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request`
        WITHIN 5
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company neither complied with the request nor applied to the court within five working days")
    ROR
    (   PARTY Company
        MUST `s 117(1)(b) the company applies to the court`
        WITHIN 5
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company neither complied with the request nor applied to the court within five working days")

-- src:1576 | (2) If it applies to the court it must notify the person making the request.
@ref s 117(2) Notifying the person making the request (src:1576)
GIVEN `the company applies to the court under section 117` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(2) the company must notify the person making the request` MEANS
    IF `the company applies to the court under section 117`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it applies to the court it must notify the person making the request"

-- src:1577 | (3) If on an application under this section the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose—
-- src:1578 | (a) it shall direct the company not to comply with the request, and
-- src:1579 | (b) it may further order that the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on the application be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request, even if he is not a party to the application.
@ref s 117(3) Directions and costs on an application (src:1577-1579)
GIVEN `an application is made under section 117` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(3)(a) the court shall direct the company not to comply with the request` MEANS
    IF `an application is made under section 117` AND `the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under this section the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose"

@ref s 117(3)(b) The court may order costs against the person who made the request (src:1577 and src:1579)
GIVEN `an application is made under section 117` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who made the request is a party to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(3)(b) the court may order the company's costs on the application to be paid in whole or in part by the person who made the request` MEANS
    IF `an application is made under section 117` AND `the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "even if he is not a party to the application": whether the person is a party makes no difference
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If on an application under this section the court is satisfied that the inspection or copy is not sought for a proper purpose" (a grant or power with an "If" gate; fork F20)

-- src:1580 | (4) If the court makes such a direction and it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose (whether made by the same person or different persons), it may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request.
@ref s 117(4) A direction as to other requests made for a similar purpose (src:1580)
GIVEN `the court makes a direction under section 117(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(4) the court may direct that the company is not to comply with any such request` MEANS
    IF `the court makes a direction under section 117(3)(a)` AND `it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court makes such a direction and it appears to the court that the company is or may be subject to other requests made for a similar purpose" (a grant or power with an "If" gate; fork F21)

-- src:1581 | The order must contain such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies.
@ref s 117(4) The order must identify the requests to which it applies (src:1581)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under section 117(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(4) the order must contain provision to identify the requests to which it applies` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under section 117(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The order must contain such provision as appears to the court appropriate to identify the requests to which it applies" (the sentence is about the order of s 117(4))

-- src:1582 | (5) If on an application under this section the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request, the company must comply with the request immediately upon the court giving its decision or, as the case may be, the proceedings being discontinued.
@ref s 117(5) Complying with the request when the court does not direct otherwise (src:1582)
GIVEN `on an application under section 117 the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has given its decision or the proceedings have been discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(5) the company must comply with the request immediately` MEANS
    IF NOT `on an application under section 117 the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under this section the court does not direct the company not to comply with the request"
    ELSE IF `the court has given its decision or the proceedings have been discontinued`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "immediately upon the court giving its decision or, as the case may be, the proceedings being discontinued" ("upon" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

-- ---- s 118: refusal of inspection or default in providing a copy ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1583 | 118 Register of members: refusal of inspection or default in providing copy
-- src:1584 | (1) If an inspection required under section 116 (register of members: right to inspect and require copy) is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section, otherwise than in accordance with an order of the court, an offence is committed by—
-- src:1585 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1586 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 118(1) Offence: refusal of inspection or default in providing a copy (src:1583-1586)
GIVEN `an inspection required under section 116 is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refusal or default is in accordance with an order of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `an inspection required under section 116 is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an inspection required under section 116 ... is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section ... an offence is committed by"
    ELSE IF `the refusal or default is in accordance with an order of the court`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "otherwise than in accordance with an order of the court"
         ELSE `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` person `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:1587 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 118(2) Penalty (src:1587)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 118(2) the penalty for an offence under s 118` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- src:1588 | (3) In the case of any such refusal or default the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or, as the case may be, direct that the copy required be sent to the person requesting it.
@ref s 118(3) The court may compel inspection or direct that the copy be sent (src:1588)
GIVEN `an inspection required under section 116 is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118(3) the court may by order compel an immediate inspection or direct that the copy required be sent to the person requesting it` MEANS
    IF `an inspection required under section 116 is refused or default is made in providing a copy required under that section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of any such refusal or default the court may by order compel an immediate inspection"

-- ---- s 119: offences in connection with a request or the disclosure of information ---------------------------------------------

-- src:1589 | 119 Register of members: offences in connection with request for or disclosure of information
-- src:1590 | (1) It is an offence for a person knowingly or recklessly to make in a request under section 116 (register of members: right to inspect or require copy) a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
@ref s 119(1) Offence: a false statement in a request (src:1589-1590)
GIVEN `the person makes in a request under section 116 a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes the statement knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes the statement recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(1) the person commits an offence by a false statement in a request` MEANS
    IF `the person makes in a request under section 116 a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` AND (`the person makes the statement knowingly` OR `the person makes the statement recklessly`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person knowingly or recklessly to make in a request under section 116 ... a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular"

-- src:1591 | (2) It is an offence for a person in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by that section—
-- src:1592 | (a) to do anything that results in the information being disclosed to another person, or
-- src:1593 | (b) to fail to do anything with the result that the information is disclosed to another person,
-- src:1594 | knowing, or having reason to suspect, that person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose.
@ref s 119(2) Offence: disclosing the information for an improper purpose (src:1591-1594)
GIVEN `the person is in possession of information obtained by exercise of a right conferred by section 116` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does something that results in the information being disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to do something with the result that the information is disclosed to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows, or has reason to suspect, that the other person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(2) the person commits an offence by disclosure` MEANS
    IF       `the person is in possession of information obtained by exercise of a right conferred by section 116`
         AND (`the person does something that results in the information being disclosed to another person` OR `the person fails to do something with the result that the information is disclosed to another person`)
         AND `the person knows, or has reason to suspect, that the other person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person in possession of information obtained by exercise of either of the rights conferred by that section ... knowing, or having reason to suspect, that person may use the information for a purpose that is not a proper purpose"

-- src:1595 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:1596 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:1597 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:1598 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:1599 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 119(3) Penalties (src:1595-1599)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 119(3) the penalty for an offence under s 119` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text distinguishes summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland and in Northern Ireland

-- ---- s 120: information as to the state of the register and index ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1600 | 120 Information as to state of register and index
-- src:1601 | (1) When a person inspects the register, or the company provides him with a copy of the register or any part of it, the company must inform him of the most recent date (if any) on which alterations were made to the register and whether there are further alterations to be made.
@ref s 120(1) Information as to the state of the register (src:1600-1601)
GIVEN `the person inspects the register, or the company provides the person with a copy of the register or any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration relates to information that the company is required to refrain from disclosing by virtue of regulations under section 120A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120(1) the company must inform the person of the most recent date on which alterations were made and whether further alterations are to be made` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person inspects the register, or the company provides the person with a copy of the register or any part of it`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a person inspects the register, or the company provides him with a copy of the register or any part of it" ("when" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    ELSE IF `the alteration relates to information that the company is required to refrain from disclosing by virtue of regulations under section 120A`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to an alteration that relates to information that the company is required to refrain from disclosing" (s 120(2A))
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 120(1) Information as to the state of the register (src:1601)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 114 act under Chapter 2 of Part 8`
`s 120(1) the company must inform the person of the most recent date of alteration (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 120(1) the company informs the person of the most recent date of alteration`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not inform the person of the most recent date on which alterations were made to the register"

-- src:1602 | (2) When a person inspects the index of members' names, the company must inform him whether there is any alteration to the register that is not reflected in the index.
-- src:1603 | (2A) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to an alteration that relates to information that the company is required to refrain from disclosing by virtue of regulations under section 120A (protected material).
