      `the alteration relates to information that the company is required to refrain from disclosing by virtue of regulations under section 120A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120(2) the company must inform the person whether there is any alteration to the register that is not reflected in the index` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person inspects the index of members' names`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a person inspects the index of members' names" ("when" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    ELSE IF `the alteration relates to information that the company is required to refrain from disclosing by virtue of regulations under section 120A`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to an alteration that relates to information that the company is required to refrain from disclosing" (s 120(2A))
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1604 | (3) If a company fails to provide the information required under subsection (1) or (2), an offence is committed by—
-- src:1605 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1606 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
