-- src:1631 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:1632 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:1633 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 120B(2) Penalties (src:1631-1633)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 120B(2) the penalty for an offence under s 120B` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text distinguishes summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland and in Northern Ireland
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists summary conviction and says nothing of conviction on indictment

