-- "after the expiration of ten years from the date": a period "from" a date does not count that day (fork F9), so the
-- period ends with the tenth anniversary and the first day after it is the first day on which removal may happen.
-- src:1635 | 121 Removal of entries relating to former members
-- src:1636 | An entry relating to a former member of the company may be removed from the register after the expiration of ten years from the date on which he ceased to be a member.
@ref s 121 Removal of entries relating to former members (src:1635-1636)
GIVEN `the entry relates to a former member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the person ceased to be a member` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the entry is removed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121 the entry relating to the former member may be removed from the register` MEANS
    IF NOT `the entry relates to a former member of the company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An entry relating to a former member of the company"
    ELSE IF `the date on which the entry is removed` GREATER THAN `add years` `the date on which the person ceased to be a member` 10
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be removed from the register after the expiration of ten years from the date on which he ceased to be a member" ("after" is an "until" bar: ruling of 2026-11-05 (d))

-- ---- s 122: share warrants ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1639 | (1) Until a share warrant issued by a company is surrendered the following are deemed to be the particulars required to be entered in the register of members in respect of the warrant—
-- src:1640 | (a) the fact of the issue of the warrant,
-- src:1641 | (b) a statement of the shares included in the warrant, distinguishing each share by its number so long as the share has a number, and
-- src:1642 | (c) the date of the issue of the warrant.
@ref s 122(1) The particulars deemed to be required (src:1639-1642)
DECLARE `s 122(1) particular of a share warrant` IS ONE OF
    `s 122(1)(a) the fact of the issue of the warrant`
    `s 122(1)(b) a statement of the shares included in the warrant`
    `s 122(1)(c) the date of the issue of the warrant`
    `s 122(1) another particular`

-- src:1638 | 122 Share warrants
-- src:1639 | (1) Until a share warrant issued by a company is surrendered the following are deemed to be the particulars required to be entered in the register of members in respect of the warrant—
-- src:1640 | (a) the fact of the issue of the warrant,
-- src:1641 | (b) a statement of the shares included in the warrant, distinguishing each share by its number so long as the share has a number, and
-- src:1642 | (c) the date of the issue of the warrant.
@ref s 122(1) Share warrants: the particulars deemed to be required (src:1638-1642)
GIVEN `the share warrant has been surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      particular IS A `s 122(1) particular of a share warrant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(1) the particular is deemed to be required to be entered in the register of members in respect of the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the share warrant has been surrendered`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Until a share warrant issued by a company is surrendered the following are deemed to be the particulars required to be entered"
    ELSE CONSIDER particular
         WHEN `s 122(1)(a) the fact of the issue of the warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 122(1)(b) a statement of the shares included in the warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 122(1)(c) the date of the issue of the warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 122(1) another particular` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): other particulars may be required by other provisions of s 113

@ref s 122(1)(b) The statement of shares distinguishes each share by its number (src:1640-1641)
GIVEN `the share warrant has been surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share has a number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(1)(b) the statement of the shares must distinguish the share by its number` MEANS
    IF `the share warrant has been surrendered`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Until a share warrant issued by a company is surrendered"
    ELSE IF `the share has a number`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "distinguishing each share by its number so long as the share has a number"

-- s 122(2) does not appear in this text (the numbering goes from (1) to (3)); s 122(4) is blank.
-- src:1643 | (3) The bearer of a share warrant may, if the articles of the company so provide, be deemed a member of the company within the meaning of this Act, either to the full extent or for any purposes defined in the articles.
@ref s 122(3) The bearer of a share warrant may be deemed a member (src:1643)
GIVEN `the articles of the company so provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(3) the bearer of a share warrant may be deemed a member of the company, to the full extent or for the purposes the articles define` MEANS
    IF `the articles of the company so provide`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, if the articles of the company so provide, be deemed a member of the company" (a grant or power with an "if" gate; fork F22)

-- src:1645 | (5) The company is responsible for any loss incurred by any person by reason of the company entering in the register the name of a bearer of a share warrant in respect of the shares specified in it without the warrant being surrendered and cancelled.
@ref s 122(5) The company's responsibility for loss (src:1645)
GIVEN `the company entered in the register the name of a bearer of a share warrant in respect of the shares specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant had been surrendered and cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person incurred loss by reason of that entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(5) the company is responsible for the person's loss` MEANS
    IF       `the company entered in the register the name of a bearer of a share warrant in respect of the shares specified in it`
         AND (NOT `the warrant had been surrendered and cancelled`)
         AND `the person incurred loss by reason of that entry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The company is responsible for any loss incurred by any person by reason of the company entering in the register the name of a bearer of a share warrant in respect of the shares specified in it without the warrant being surrendered and cancelled"

-- src:1646 | (6) On the surrender of a share warrant, the date of the surrender must be entered in the register.
