-- src:1649 | (2) If the number of members of a limited company falls to one, or if an unlimited company with only one member becomes a limited company on re-registration, there shall upon the occurrence of that event be entered in the company's register of members , with the name and address of the sole member—
-- src:1650 | (a) a statement that the company has only one member, and
-- src:1651 | (b) the date on which the company became a company having only one member.
@ref s 123(2) The number of members falls to one (src:1649-1651)
GIVEN `the number of members of a limited company falls to one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an unlimited company with only one member becomes a limited company on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(2) the register must contain a statement that the company has only one member and the date on which it became a company having only one member` MEANS
    IF `the number of members of a limited company falls to one` OR `an unlimited company with only one member becomes a limited company on re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the number of members of a limited company falls to one, or if an unlimited company with only one member becomes a limited company on re-registration, there shall upon the occurrence of that event be entered"

-- src:1652 | (3) If the membership of a limited company increases from one to two or more members, there shall upon the occurrence of that event be entered in the company's register of members , with the name and address of the person who was formerly the sole member—
-- src:1653 | (a) a statement that the company has ceased to have only one member, and
-- src:1654 | (b) the date on which that event occurred.
@ref s 123(3) The membership increases from one to two or more (src:1652-1654)
GIVEN `the membership of a limited company increases from one to two or more members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(3) the register must contain a statement that the company has ceased to have only one member and the date on which that event occurred` MEANS
    IF `the membership of a limited company increases from one to two or more members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the membership of a limited company increases from one to two or more members, there shall upon the occurrence of that event be entered"

-- src:1655 | (4) If a company makes default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:1656 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1657 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 123(4) Offence (src:1655-1657)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with section 123` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company makes default in complying with section 123`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` person `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:1658 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 123(5) Penalty (src:1658)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 123(5) the penalty for an offence under s 123` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- ---- s 124: treasury shares -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1659 | 124 Company holding its own shares as treasury shares
-- src:1660 | (1) Where a company purchases its own shares in circumstances in which section 724 (treasury shares) applies—
-- src:1661 | (a) the requirements of section 113 (register of members) need not be complied with if the company cancels all of the shares forthwith after the purchase, and
@ref s 124(1)(a) A company purchases its own shares: section 113 need not be complied with (src:1659-1661)
GIVEN `the company purchases its own shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 724 section 724 (treasury shares) applies to the purchase` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company cancels all of the shares forthwith after the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124(1)(a) the requirements of section 113 need not be complied with` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company purchases its own shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company purchases its own shares"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 724 section 724 (treasury shares) applies to the purchase`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in circumstances in which section 724 (treasury shares) applies"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 724 is not among the sources
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the company cancels all of the shares forthwith after the purchase`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not be complied with if the company cancels all of the shares forthwith after the purchase"

-- src:1659 | 124 Company holding its own shares as treasury shares
-- src:1662 | (b) if the company does not cancel all of the shares forthwith after the purchase, any share that is so cancelled shall be disregarded for the purposes of that section.
@ref s 124(1)(b) Shares cancelled when not all are cancelled forthwith (src:1659 and src:1662)
GIVEN `the company purchases its own shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 724 section 724 (treasury shares) applies to the purchase` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company cancels all of the shares forthwith after the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share is so cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124(1)(b) the share is disregarded for the purposes of section 113` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company purchases its own shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company purchases its own shares"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 724 section 724 (treasury shares) applies to the purchase`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in circumstances in which section 724 (treasury shares) applies"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 724 is not among the sources
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the company cancels all of the shares forthwith after the purchase`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company does not cancel all of the shares forthwith after the purchase"
             ELSE IF `the share is so cancelled`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any share that is so cancelled shall be disregarded"

-- src:1663 | (2) Subject to subsection (1), where a company holds shares as treasury shares the company must be entered in the register as the member holding those shares.
@ref s 124(2) The company is entered as the member holding treasury shares (src:1663)
GIVEN `the company holds shares as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 124(2) the company must be entered in the register as the member holding those shares` MEANS
    IF `the company holds shares as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a company holds shares as treasury shares the company must be entered in the register as the member holding those shares" ("Subject to subsection (1)": fork F10)

-- ---- s 125: power of the court to rectify the register ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1669 | the person aggrieved, or any member of the company, or the company, may apply to the court for rectification of the register.
@ref s 125(1) Who may apply for rectification (src:1669)
DECLARE `s 125(1) applicant for rectification` IS ONE OF
    `s 125(1) the person aggrieved`
    `s 125(1) any member of the company`
    `s 125(1) the company`
    `s 125(1) someone else`

-- src:1665 | 125 Power of court to rectify register
-- src:1666 | (1) If a company’s register of members—
-- src:1667 | (a) does not include information that it is required to include, or
-- src:1668 | (b) includes information that it is not required to include,
-- src:1669 | the person aggrieved, or any member of the company, or the company, may apply to the court for rectification of the register.
@ref s 125(1) Who may apply for rectification (src:1665-1669)
GIVEN `the register does not include information that it is required to include` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register includes information that it is not required to include` IS A BOOLEAN
      applicant IS A `s 125(1) applicant for rectification`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(1) the applicant may apply to the court for rectification of the register` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the register does not include information that it is required to include` OR `the register includes information that it is not required to include`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a company’s register of members— (a) does not include information that it is required to include, or (b) includes information that it is not required to include, the person aggrieved, or any member of the company, or the company, may apply to the court for rectification of the register" (a grant or power with an "If" gate; fork F23)
    ELSE CONSIDER applicant
         WHEN `s 125(1) the person aggrieved` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 125(1) any member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 125(1) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 125(1) someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the person aggrieved, any member and the company, and says nothing of anyone else

-- src:1670 | (2) The court may either refuse the application or may order rectification of the register and payment by the company of any damages sustained by any party aggrieved.
@ref s 125(2) The orders the court may make (src:1670)
DECLARE `s 125(2) order of the court on an application for rectification` IS ONE OF
    `s 125(2) refuse the application`
    `s 125(2) order rectification of the register`
    `s 125(2) order payment by the company of any damages sustained by any party aggrieved`
    `s 125(2) another order`

-- src:1670 | (2) The court may either refuse the application or may order rectification of the register and payment by the company of any damages sustained by any party aggrieved.
@ref s 125(2) The court may refuse or order rectification and damages (src:1670)
GIVEN `an application for rectification has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `s 125(2) order of the court on an application for rectification`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(2) the court may make the order` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application for rectification has been made`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 125(2) speaks of the court's powers on the application of s 125(1)
    ELSE CONSIDER order
         WHEN `s 125(2) refuse the application` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 125(2) order rectification of the register` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 125(2) order payment by the company of any damages sustained by any party aggrieved` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 125(2) another order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names refusal, rectification and damages, and says nothing of other orders

-- src:1671 | (3) On such an application the court may decide any question relating to the title of a person who is a party to the application to have his name entered in or omitted from the register, whether the question arises between members or alleged members, or between members or alleged members on the one hand and the company on the other hand, and generally may decide any question necessary or expedient to be decided for rectification of the register.
@ref s 125(3) Questions the court may decide (src:1671)
GIVEN `the question arises on an application under section 125` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question relates to the title of a party to the application to have a name entered in or omitted from the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is necessary or expedient to be decided for rectification of the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(3) the court may decide the question` MEANS
    IF NOT `the question arises on an application under section 125`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On such an application the court may decide any question"
    ELSE IF `the question relates to the title of a party to the application to have a name entered in or omitted from the register` OR `the question is necessary or expedient to be decided for rectification of the register`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any question relating to the title of a person who is a party to the application ... and generally ... any question necessary or expedient to be decided for rectification of the register"

-- src:1672 | (4) In the case of a company required by this Act to send a list of its members to the registrar of companies, the court, when making an order for rectification of the register, shall by its order direct notice of the rectification to be given to the registrar.
@ref s 125(4) Notice of the rectification to the registrar (src:1672)
GIVEN `the company is required by this Act to send a list of its members to the registrar of companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court makes an order for rectification of the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125(4) the court shall by its order direct notice of the rectification to be given to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the company is required by this Act to send a list of its members to the registrar of companies` AND `the court makes an order for rectification of the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a company required by this Act to send a list of its members to the registrar of companies, the court, when making an order for rectification of the register, shall by its order direct notice"

-- ---- s 126: trusts not to be entered on the register ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1673 | 126 Trusts not to be entered on register
-- src:1674 | No notice of any trust, expressed, implied or constructive, shall be entered on the register of members of a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, or be receivable by the registrar.
@ref s 126 Trusts not to be entered on register (src:1673-1674)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the notice is of a trust, expressed, implied or constructive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126 notice of a trust may be entered on the register of members or be received by the registrar` MEANS
    IF NOT `the notice is of a trust, expressed, implied or constructive`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No notice of any trust, expressed, implied or constructive"
    ELSE CONSIDER place
         WHEN `England and Wales` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No notice of any trust, expressed, implied or constructive, shall be entered on the register of members of a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, or be receivable by the registrar"
         WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No notice of any trust, expressed, implied or constructive, shall be entered on the register of members of a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, or be receivable by the registrar"
         WHEN Scotland THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of a company registered in England and Wales or Northern Ireland"

-- ---- s 127: the register to be evidence ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1676 | (1) The register of members is prima facie evidence of any matters which are by this Act directed or authorised to be inserted in it , except for any matters of which the central register is prima facie evidence by virtue of subsection (2).
@ref s 127(1) The register of members is prima facie evidence (src:1676)
GIVEN `the matter is directed or authorised by this Act to be inserted in the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the central register is prima facie evidence of the matter by virtue of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(1) the register of members is prima facie evidence of the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT `the matter is directed or authorised by this Act to be inserted in the register of members`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any matters which are by this Act directed or authorised to be inserted in it"
    ELSE IF `the central register is prima facie evidence of the matter by virtue of subsection (2)`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for any matters of which the central register is prima facie evidence by virtue of subsection (2)"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1677 | (2) The central register is prima facie evidence of any matters about which a company was required to deliver information to the registrar under Chapter 2A by virtue of an election under section 128B at any time before the repeal of that Chapter (including that section) by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023.
@ref s 127(2) The central register is prima facie evidence (src:1677)
GIVEN `the company was required to deliver information about the matter to the registrar under Chapter 2A by virtue of an election under section 128B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that requirement arose at a time before the repeal of Chapter 2A by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
