`s 127(2) the central register is prima facie evidence of the matter` MEANS
    IF `the company was required to deliver information about the matter to the registrar under Chapter 2A by virtue of an election under section 128B` AND `that requirement arose at a time before the repeal of Chapter 2A by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any matters about which a company was required to deliver information to the registrar under Chapter 2A by virtue of an election under section 128B at any time before the repeal of that Chapter"

-- src:1678 | (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to information required to be included in a statement under section 128B(5)(b) or in any updated statement under section 128B(6) before their repeal by that Act.
@ref s 127(3) Information in statements under s 128B(5)(b) or (6) (src:1678)
GIVEN `the information is required to be included in a statement under section 128B(5)(b) or in an updated statement under section 128B(6) before their repeal by that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(3) subsection (2) applies to the information` MEANS
    IF `the information is required to be included in a statement under section 128B(5)(b) or in an updated statement under section 128B(6) before their repeal by that Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply to information required to be included in a statement under section 128B(5)(b) or in any updated statement under section 128B(6) before their repeal by that Act"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 127(3) says only that subsection (2) does not apply to that information; for other information s 127(2) decides

-- src:1679 | (4) In this section “the central register” means the register kept by the registrar (see section 1080).
@ref s 127(4) "the central register" (src:1679)
GIVEN `the register is the register kept by the registrar (see section 1080)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(4) the register is the central register` MEANS
    IF `the register is the register kept by the registrar (see section 1080)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “the central register” means the register kept by the registrar"

-- ---- s 128: time limit for claims arising from entry in register -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1680 | 128 Time limit for claims arising from entry in register
-- src:1681 | (1) Liability incurred by a company—
-- src:1682 | (a) from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of members, or
-- src:1683 | (b) from a failure to make or delete any such entry,
-- src:1684 | is not enforceable more than ten years after the date on which the entry was made or deleted or, as the case may be, the failure first occurred.
@ref s 128(1) Liability not enforceable more than ten years after (src:1680-1684)
GIVEN `the liability was incurred by the company from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of members, or from a failure to make or delete such an entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the entry was made or deleted or the failure first occurred` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the liability is sought to be enforced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(1) the liability is not enforceable` MEANS
    IF NOT `the liability was incurred by the company from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of members, or from a failure to make or delete such an entry`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Liability incurred by a company— (a) from the making or deletion of an entry in the register of members, or (b) from a failure to make or delete any such entry"
    ELSE IF `the date on which the liability is sought to be enforced` GREATER THAN `add years` `the date on which the entry was made or deleted or the failure first occurred` 10
         THEN JUST TRUE -- the text: "is not enforceable more than ten years after the date" (a day more than ten years after: fork F9)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence says only that the liability is not enforceable more than ten years after; within ten years it says nothing

-- src:1685 | (2) This is without prejudice to any lesser period of limitation (and, in Scotland, to any rule that the obligation giving rise to the liability prescribes before the expiry of that period).
@ref s 128(2) Without prejudice to a lesser period (src:1685)
GIVEN `a lesser period of limitation applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is registered in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a rule applies that the obligation giving rise to the liability prescribes before the expiry of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(2) s 128(1) leaves a shorter period of limitation or prescription in force` MEANS
    IF `a lesser period of limitation applies` OR (`the company is registered in Scotland` AND `a rule applies that the obligation giving rise to the liability prescribes before the expiry of that period`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without prejudice to any lesser period of limitation (and, in Scotland, to any rule that the obligation ... prescribes before the expiry of that period)"

-- ---- s 128ZA: transitional provision where information kept on central register ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1686 | 128ZA Transitional provision where information kept on central register
