`s 128ZA(1)(a) the company must enter in its register of members all of the information that it would have had to enter if the election had never been made` MEANS
    IF `an election was made under section 128B at a time before the repeal of that section by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an election is made under section 128B (option to keep information on central register) at any time before the repeal of that section"

@ref s 128ZA(1)(b) The duty is treated as imposed by the provision that would have required the entry (src:1686 and src:1689)
GIVEN `an election was made under section 128B at a time before the repeal of that section by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
